{title: 148 - O Love, How Deep, How Broad}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #148 • INFINITE LOVE • 8.7.8.8}
{lyricist: Thomas a Kempis j}
{composer: James Bingham}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 148}
{meta: tune INFINITE LOVE}
{meta: meter 8.7.8.8}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]O [Am]love, [F]how [Dm]deep, [F]how [Bb]broad, [C7]how [Am]high,
[F]Beyond [Dm]all [C7/Bb]thought and [Am/E]fantasy,
[F]That [Dm]God, [Bb/F]the [Edim]Son [Am/E]of God, [Dm/A]should take
[C]Our mortal [Dm]form [Am]for [Gm]mortal's [C7/Bb]sake!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]For [Am]us [F]baptized, for [Bb]us [C7]He [Am]bore
[F]His [Dm]holy [C7/Bb]fast and [Am/E]hungered [F]sore;
[F]For [Dm]us [Bb/F]temptation [Am/E]sharp [Dm/A]He knew;
[C]For us [F]the [Dm]tempter [Gm]over [C7/Bb]threw.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]For [Am]us [F]by [Dm]wickedness [C7]betrayed,
[F]For [Dm]us, [C7/Bb]in crown [Am/E]of [Gm]thorns [F]arrayed,
[F]He [Dm]bore [Bb/F]the shameful [F]cross [Dm/A]and death;
[C]For us [F]He [Bb]gave [Am]His [Gm]dying [C7/Bb]breath.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]For [Am]us [F]He [Dm]rose [F]from [Bb]death [C7]again,
[F]For [Dm]us [C7/Bb]He went on [Am/E]high [Gm]to [F]reign;
[F]For [Dm]us [Bb/F]He [Edim]sent [Am/E]His Spirit [Dm/A]here
[C]To guide, [F]to [Dm]strengthen, [Gm]and [F]to [C7/Bb]cheer.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[C]All [Am]glory [Dm]to [F]our [Bb]Lord [C7]and [Am]God
[F]For [Dm]love [C7/Bb]so deep, so [Am/E]high, [Gm]so [F]broad;
[F]The [Dm]Trinity [Am/E]whom we [Dm/A]adore
[C]Forever [Dm]and [Am]forevermore.
{end_of_verse}
